    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=1,\\ b=5,\\ c=2$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{37}{13}&=2+\\frac{11}{13}\\\\\na+\\frac{1}{b+\\dfrac{1}{c}}&=\\frac{1}{\\dfrac{11}{13}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{13}{11}\\\\\n&=1+\\frac{2}{11}\n\\end{align*}$$\nThus $a=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{1}{b+\\dfrac{1}{c}}&=\\frac{2}{11}\\\\\nb+\\frac{1}{c}&=\\frac{11}{2}\\\\\n&=5+\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{align*}$$\nHence $b=5$ and $c=2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
